<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <.head title="Colophon" {assigns} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <.nav {assigns} />

    <main>
      <h1>Colophon</h1>

      <p>
        This site was handcoded using Neovim, the perfect hammer for an imperfect world. Best viewed in any browser, including Firefox, Netscape Navigator, Internet Explorer and lynx. 
      </p>

      <p>
        All original content on this website is freely available in the <a href="//stpeter.im/writings/essays/publicdomain.html">public domain</a> in accordance with the <a href="//creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0 Universal license</a>. Download, copy, remix all allowed.
      </p>

      <p>
        The source code is available on <a href="//github.com/RobinBoers/geheimesite.nl">GitHub</a>, <a href="//codeberg.org/RobinBoers/geheimesite.nl">Codeberg</a> and <a href="//git.dupunkto.org/~sites/geheimesite.nl">Gitz</a>, and is licensed AGPLv3 because I strongly believe in Copyleft. 
      </p>

      <p>
        A lot of effort was spent on perfecting the server configuration. It currently does HTTP3, HSTS, CSP, Brotli compression, indefinite caching for assets and daily caching for content. A <a href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a> file is autogenerated nightly with the help of <a href="//darkvisitors.com">Dark Visitors</a> in a futile attempt to block AI spiders from relentlessly scraping my site.
      </p>

      <p>
        The site primarily uses your system font stack. All other fonts (on other subdomains) are self-hosted <a href="//brycewray.com/posts/2020/08/google-fonts-privacy/">to prevent Google from tracking my visitors</a>.
      </p>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <.footer />
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>